# https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The level of accuracy for an axis mapping."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Accuracy"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Axis Mapping is related to an Appearance of an Entity Space\r\n    and defines which Axis of the Entity Space (Source Axis) can be mapped to which Axis of the Reference Space\r\n     (another Entity, Document or Asset Space). This relation can be further specified with an accuracy.\r\n     An AxisMapping object can only relate on Source Axis to one Reference Axis.\r\n     Thus, typically, each Entity Space Appearance links to three Axis Mapping objects."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Axis Mapping"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisRelationType
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisRelationType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisRelationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Defines the geometrical relation between two mapped axes."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisRelationType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Axis Relation Type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A point that defines a boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis. "@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Boundary Point"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Boundary Point Mapping describes the relation of an Entity Axis Boundary Point (Source Point)\r\n        to the reference space. The relation can be expressed by Directional Properties of the RELOC Ontology\r\n        (e.g., containedInFront/Right/Bottom etc.)  in relation to the reference space.\r\n "@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPointMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Boundary Point Mapping"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A point that represents the maximum/upper boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MaxBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Maximum Boundary Point"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#BoundaryPoint> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A point that represents the minimum/lower boundary of an Entity Space on a specific Axis "@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#MinBoundaryPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Minimum Boundary Point"@en .
