# https://w3id.org/spot/am#Antiparallel
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Antiparallel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Antiparallel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#AxisRelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Antiparallel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The source axis is antiparallel (parallel but directed in opposite direction) to the target axis."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Antiparallel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Antiparallel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Antiparallel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://www.oed.com/dictionary/antiparallel_adj> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#Approximate
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Approximate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Approximate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Approximate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The relationship between the axes defined in the axis mapping corresponds closely to reality, with minor deviations (e.g., nearly parallel axes)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Approximate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Approximate"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#Broad
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Broad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Broad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/spot/am#Accuracy> .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Broad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The source axis is assigned to the closest matching target axis in the context of the defined relationship, despite significant discrepancies."@en .
<https://w3id.org/spot/am#Broad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Broad"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/spot/am#Codirectional
